Xingzhou / 星舟 — public source edition

The Chaoxing backend is derived from Samueli924/chaoxing v3.1.4:
https://github.com/Samueli924/chaoxing
Its GNU GPL version 3 license is retained in LICENSE and
chaoxing-3.1.4/LICENSE. Existing author and source notices are retained.

This distribution adds and maintains the authenticated service backend,
independent Go web console, related tests, and Linux operating instructions.
The initial public snapshot was prepared on 2026-11-21. Publication-only
changes include the Xingzhou name, a generic initial owner username,
sanitized configuration templates, isolated offline test fixtures, and
independent build/run documentation.

Lucide's bundled JavaScript is distributed under its own ISC license.
See server-web/internal/server/static/LICENSE for the complete notice.
Other Go/Python dependencies retain their respective upstream licenses.

No account database, learning history, API key, session cookie, production
deployment configuration, or prebuilt executable is included.
